    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/charge-chargee-de-scolarite-m2-53c144": {
      "title": "Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H",
      "description": "Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H - Temporary contract 6 months in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Apply to this job Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H I apply Published on               \n                02/09/2026 Contract type: Temporary contract\n- 6 months Work time: Full time Location Paris L'entreprise ESCP Business School Paris est l'école de commerce de renommée mondiale, fondée en 1819, qui forme les leaders responsables de demain. Ancrée au cœur de Paris, elle propose une pédagogie innovante et multiculturelle, s’appuyant sur un réseau de six campus européens. Reconnue pour l’excellence de ses programmes en management, elle favorise l’engagement, l’ouverture internationale et l’accompagnement personnalisé des talents tout au long de leur parcours. Description du poste Vous êtes en charge : ● De la gestion des cours, des contrôles terminaux et des résultats ● De la gestion administrative des intervenants et le suivi des heures enseignées ● Du suivi de certains groupes spécifiques d’étudiants, notamment des étudiants en apprentissage et/ou étudiants en filière classique Master 2 ● De l’organisation de séminaires, déplacements des étudiants en fonction de leur cursus ● Vous participez à la préparation des comités de suivi pédagogique ● Vous renseignez les étudiants sur leurs parcours et vous assurez du respect de leurs obligations académiques, de leur assiduité ● Vous êtes l’interlocuteur privilégié des départements d’enseignement et des professeurs pour le bon déroulement des cours ● En fonction de la population d’étudiants suivis vous pouvez être en relation avec des entreprises partenaires, maîtres d’apprentissage, RH ● Vous participez aux grands évènements du cycle de scolarité (Rentrée, Cérémonie de remise des diplômes, Séminaires …) ● Vous participez, contribuez, soutenez l’activité de l’ensemble du service et de la direction en fonction des besoins. ● Vous participez aux audits Qualiopi Profil recherché Diplômé d’un Bac +3 ou équivalent, vous justifiez d’une expérience professionnelle significative de 2 ans au minimum dans un contexte interculturel (+60% étudiants internationaux). Une expérience internationale est un atout. Vos capacités d'organisation, votre rigueur, votre sens du service, votre esprit d’équipe seront très appréciés. Un intérêt et une aisance dans l’utilisation des outils numériques et système d’information sont indispensables. D’excellentes qualités relationnelles et le sens du service client vous assureront de remplir ces missions avec succès. Vous maîtrisez parfaitement l’anglais et le français, à l’écrit et à l’oral (nombreux échanges avec les étudiants et les collègues dans les deux langues). Vous maîtrisez parfaitement les outils bureautiques (Word, Excel, Bases de données). Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 53c144c5-27c9-41c5-b491-451eb7b37be3 Apply Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Temporary contract - 6 months Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Pourquoi souhaitez vous rejoindre ESCP Business School ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Temporary contract\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply Communications Intern (3–6 months) F/H Internship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H Permanent contract Full time Levallois-Perret I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
    },
    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/program-officer--apprenticeship-e0dd30": {
      "title": "Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H",
      "description": "Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H - Apprenticeship 12 months in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apply to this job Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H I apply Published on               \n                02/09/2026 Contract type: Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description As part of the development of its activities at the Dubai Campus, ESCP Business School is looking for a Program officer to contribute to the coordination and operational management of programmes delivered in Dubai, as well as other projects related to Executive Education. Reporting to the Project Manager within the Executive Education team, the Program officer will work in an international and multi-campus environment. The role involves close collaboration with ESCP’s internal teams, faculty members and the various stakeholders involved in the delivery and monitoring of programmes. The position requires strong organisational skills and the ability to coordinate cross-functional activities while managing practical operational and administrative tasks to ensure the smooth delivery of activities at the Dubai Campus. MAIN RESPONSIBILITIES Ensure the operational monitoring and follow-up of ongoing projects and activities. Manage programme administration tools and processes, including grade entry, diploma printing, certificates of achievement and related administrative tasks. Provide coordination support to faculty members, the Programme team and support functions, including the use of Aurion and Canvas LMS. Ensure effective follow-up and support of programme participants. Contribute to the logistical and administrative organisation of training sessions. Update management tools, dashboards and reporting documents, including documentation related to accreditations. Identify operational issues and bottlenecks and propose practical solutions. Contribute to the continuous improvement of programme management processes. Profile required You are currently studying towards a BTS in Management Support, a Bachelor’s degree in Management, Humanities/Literature, or an equivalent qualification, and are looking for a work-study opportunity that will allow you to develop your programme coordination and management skills in an international environment. Previous experience in a similar role or in administrative management, coordination, project management or programme support would be an advantage. The preferred work-study schedule is 3 days at ESCP and 2 days at school . SKILLS AND PERSONAL QUALITIES Excellent command of French and English , both written and spoken. Strong organisational skills, with a rigorous and methodical approach. Excellent interpersonal and verbal communication skills. Tact and diplomacy when interacting with a wide range of stakeholders. Curiosity, autonomy and initiative. Ability to work effectively in an international and multi-campus environment. Strong team spirit and an interest in coordination and collaborative work. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: e0dd306b-8519-4711-8563-6f04397b6ff3 Apply Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apprenticeship - 12 months Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est le rythme de votre alternance ecolé/entreprise ? * A partir de quelle date pouvez vous commencer votre contrat d'alternance ? * Quelle est la durée d'alternance recherchée ? * Quel est votre niveau d'anglais * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Temporary contract\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply Communications Intern (3–6 months) F/H Internship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H Permanent contract Full time Levallois-Perret I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
