    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/european-financial-controller--degree-programmes-business-unit-6a83bb": {
      "title": "European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H",
      "description": "European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H - Permanent contract in Levallois-Perret | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H Apply to this job European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H I apply Published on               \n                28/08/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Levallois-Perret The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description Within the Group Finance Department, the Financial Controller acts as the financial point of reference for the Degree Programmes Business Unit (Bachelor, Master in Management, MSc, MBA). In a multi-campus and international environment, he/she acts as a business partner to the Academic Management team, supporting the economic steering of programmes and actively contributing to strategic decisions, with the aim of optimising performance and ensuring the sustainability of the academic model. Main Responsibilities Financial Management & Reporting Prepare, consolidate and monitor the budgets of the Degree Programmes Business Unit across all campuses. Produce monthly reporting and forecasts covering revenues, teaching costs, margins and KPIs. Analyse variances and formulate operational recommendations. Define and monitor key performance indicators, such as cost per student, profitability by programme and contribution by campus. Oversee the day-to-day budget execution of the scope, including expenditure authorisations, management of budget overruns and related matters. Academic Business Partnering Support Programme Directors and Academic Management in budget preparation and forecasting. Provide high-value-added financial analyses to inform decision-making, including cohort sizing, pricing and allocation of teaching resources. Participate in governance and steering bodies, such as programme committees and performance reviews. Forecasting & Modelling Build forecast models incorporating student recruitment dynamics and multi-campus occupancy/fill rates. Prepare business plans for programme launches, portfolio developments and academic projects. Analyse the profitability and return on investment of academic initiatives. Multi-campus Coordination & Governance Ensure financial coordination between campuses within the Degree Programmes scope. Guarantee compliance with deadlines, formats and quality standards for financial reporting across all campuses of the Academic Business Unit. Harmonise practices and contribute to data reliability, including student volumes, revenues and teaching costs. Ensure compliance with management rules and consistency with Group guidelines. Tools & Continuous Improvement Develop and improve management tools, such as dashboards, BI and models. Contribute to cross-functional projects, including ERP, academic planning tools and data initiatives. Support the increasing maturity of multi-campus financial management. Profile required Education & Experience Higher education degree in finance/management, from a business school or university. 5 to 8 years’ experience in management control. Experience in an international and matrix environment would be an advantage. Experience in business partnering is essential. Technical Skills Excellent command of professional English, with ease in using technical financial and accounting terminology, including IFRS standards, provisions, adjustments and related matters, is essential. Strong command of management control, including budgeting, forecasting and analysis. Excellent financial modelling skills. Advanced proficiency in Excel and BI tools, such as Power BI, Tableau, etc. Knowledge of an ERP system, such as SAP or Oracle, would be appreciated. Behavioural Skills Initiative. Ability to interact with and influence non-financial stakeholders. Analytical mindset, rigour and ability to prioritise. Business partner mindset, with a constructive challenge approach and solution-oriented attitude. Autonomy, proactivity and ability to coordinate in a multi-campus environment. Ability to structure and present complex information to different audiences. Success Indicators Reliability and relevance of forecasts. Compliance with deadlines and quality of multi-campus reporting. Impact of analyses on academic decisions. Improvement in the economic performance of programmes. Satisfaction of academic and financial stakeholders. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 6a83bba6-cc2f-4e81-9c4a-282b8e28a282 Apply European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H Permanent contract Full time Levallois-Perret Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Quelles sont vos motivations pour rejoindre ESCP Business school Quelle est votre compréhension du poste que nous proposons ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Temporary contract\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply Communications Intern (3–6 months) F/H Internship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H Permanent contract Full time Levallois-Perret I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
