    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/european-financial-controller--infrastructure--campus-life-5ecb82": {
      "title": "European Financial Controller – Infrastructure & Campus Life F/H",
      "description": "European Financial Controller – Infrastructure & Campus Life F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs European Financial Controller – Infrastructure & Campus Life F/H Apply to this job European Financial Controller – Infrastructure & Campus Life F/H I apply Published on               \n                28/08/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description ESCP is seeking a European Financial Controller, acting as a true Business Partner to the Infrastructure, Real Estate, IT and Campus Life departments. These areas are essential to student satisfaction, which is a decisive factor in rankings in particular. In a rapidly transforming multi-campus environment, ESCP is rolling out an investment programme of nearly €300 million over the next five years, mainly in real estate and technological infrastructure. The purpose of the role is to strengthen the financial steering of these activities by developing an integrated approach linking expenses, investments, operational performance and student experience. The scope notably covers real estate, leases, building maintenance and security, IT infrastructure, telecommunications, insurance, cleaning, living spaces and student services. Main Responsibilities Business Partner to the Real Estate, IT and Campus Life Departments Support operational departments in managing their financial performance and strategic projects. Real Estate Contribute to the European real estate strategy and campus master plan. Carry out investment analyses: acquisition versus leasing, business cases, renovations, extensions and relocations. Build forecasts, budgets and business plans, financial models and multi-year projections. Monitor budget execution, with active involvement from contract structuring through to purchase orders, delivery of works and payment of service providers. Track cost variations and propose corrective actions with the real estate teams. Analyse the economic performance of assets and monitor key indicators: cost per square metre, occupancy rate, cost per student, ROI, energy performance, and propose improvements with the Student Experience, Campus Life and Real Estate teams. Produce analyses for Executive Management and governance bodies. IT Financially steer digital transformation programmes and technology investments. Assess business cases including ROI, and monitor operating costs, licences, infrastructure and projects. Campus Life Support those responsible for student and association life in managing their resources. Challenge budgets and contribute to trade-offs between costs, service quality and student impact. Campus Life Performance Management Develop and monitor performance indicators: NPS, student satisfaction, service usage, engagement and retention. Measure the return on investment of Campus Life initiatives. Build dashboards combining financial and operational data. Identify levers to improve the student experience and economic efficiency. Investment Steering and Financial Control Contribute to the steering of the €300 million investment programme. Monitor commitments, cash outflows and budget trajectories for multi-campus projects. Assess the impact of real estate and IT investments on attractiveness and the student experience. Coordinate budget cycles and forecasts. Ensure the monitoring of budget execution, variances and action plans. Carry out forward-looking analyses and financial scenarios. Harmonisation and Continuous Improvement Harmonise management practices across campuses. Develop a performance culture combining financial results and user impact. Contribute to the development of reporting tools, ERP, BI and data analytics. Profile required Higher education degree in finance. 5 to 10 years’ experience in management control, audit or financial advisory. Fluent professional English and a strong understanding of financial issues. Strong skills in analysis, financial modelling and performance management. Ability to communicate, summarise and support decision-makers. Autonomy, rigour, proactivity and a business partner mindset. Interest in investment, real estate and transformation topics within an international environment. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 5ecb82c4-5e18-4531-9bd2-1afe133b33b2 Apply European Financial Controller – Infrastructure & Campus Life F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Quelles sont vos motivations pour rejoindre ESCP Business school Quelle est votre compréhension du poste que nous proposons ? As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Temporary contract\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Program officer – Apprenticeship F/H Apprenticeship\n- 12 months Full time Paris I apply Communications Intern (3–6 months) F/H Internship\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply European Financial Controller – Degree Programmes Business Unit F/H Permanent contract Full time Levallois-Perret I apply See more jobs Follow us Jobs Spontaneous application Useful links Terms of Use Cookies Website map Recruiters access Consent choices Powered by Applicant Tracking System"
