    "https://careers.werecruit.io/en/escp-business-school/offers/student-societies-coordinator-65a1c3": {
      "title": "Student Societies Coordinator F/H",
      "description": "Student Societies Coordinator F/H - Permanent contract in Paris | Découvrez nos offres With your agreement, We Recruit and our partners use cookies or similar technologies to store, access, and process personal data like your visit on this website, IP addresses and cookie identifiers. Some partners do not ask for your consent to process your data and rely on their legitimate business interest. You can withdraw your consent or object to data processing based on legitimate interest at any time by clicking on “Learn More” or in our Privacy Policy on this website. View our 8 partners Learn More → Disagree and close Agree and close Menu Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Plus Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP See our jobs EN EN FR Company page Espace Carrière & Mobilité des salariés ESCP Recrutement en Europe Site ESCP EN Retour EN EN FR See our jobs Student Societies Coordinator F/H Apply to this job Student Societies Coordinator F/H I apply Published on               \n                27/08/2026 Contract type: Permanent contract Work time: Full time Location Paris The company ESCP Business School is the world-renowned business school, founded in 1819, that trains the responsible leaders of tomorrow. Located in the heart of Paris, it offers innovative and multicultural teaching, supported by a network of six European campuses. Recognized for the excellence of its management programs, it fosters engagement, international awareness, and personalized support for talent throughout their studies. Post description As part of the Campus Life team, you will be responsible for the operational, administrative and regulatory management of student societies across ESCP’s Paris sites. You will support student societies in their activities and events, ensure compliance with procedures, safety requirements and applicable regulations, and contribute to an engaging, responsible and inclusive student experience. Your responsibilities: Manage the administrative follow-up of student societies and support them with their procedures and projects. Review funding applications and contribute to the management of facilities and resources made available to student societies. Support student society committees and coordinate relevant training, particularly in relation to safety and risk prevention. Coordinate student events, including scheduling, rooms, logistics, access and coordination with the relevant internal teams. Identify and anticipate event-related risks and ensure compliance with ESCP rules and procedures. Work closely with the School’s various departments and contribute to improving practices. Monitor student society activities and help promote their initiatives. Profile required Skills and experience: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree, ideally in project management, administration, events management, student affairs, communications, social sciences, management or higher education. Previous experience in project coordination, student societies or student affairs, events management or an institutional environment is preferred. Strong organisational and prioritisation skills , with particular attention to administrative accuracy. Ability to manage several projects simultaneously, identify risks and prepare the information required to support decision-making. Excellent interpersonal skills and the ability to communicate and uphold decisions clearly and diplomatically. Proficiency in monitoring and reporting tools and strong written communication skills. Required languages English - Level advanced Réf: 65a1c3a2-df2f-4dad-8ff6-af91530f47ae Apply Student Societies Coordinator F/H Permanent contract Full time Paris Title * Mrs. Mr. Mx Last name * First name * E-mail * Phone number * Availability * Select your availability immediate 2 weeks 1 month 2 months 3 months > 3 months Salary expectations (Gross/year) * Select a salary expectation Inferior than 15 000€ 15 000€ - 20 000€ 20 000€ - 25 000€ 25 000€ - 30 000€ 30 000€ - 35 000€ 35 000€ - 40 000€ 40 000€ - 45 000€ 45 000€ - 50 000€ 50 000€ - 55 000€ 55 000€ - 60 000€ 60 000€ - 65 000€ 65 000€ - 70 000€ 70 000€ - 75 000€ 75 000€ - 80 000€ 80 000€ - 85 000€ Superior than 85 000€ Photo Choose file Format: JPG \nWeight: max 2 MO. Resume * Choose file Format: .PDF,  .DOCX, .DOC. Weight: max 2 MO. Quel est votre niveau d'anglais ? * Select an answer Beginner Intermediary Advanced Bilingual Pourquoi souhaitez vous rejoindre ESCP Business School ? * As part of your application on the career site of ESCP Business School , the information you provide is processed for the review of your profile, on the basis of pre-contractual measures and the legitimate interest of the company in building a CV database. Some data may be automatically analysed (parsing and pre-screening) via an Artificial Intelligence system. No decision is made solely by AI, as every application is reviewed by a recruiter. Regarding the use of AI: - Your data is not retained by our AI solution. - It is not used to train an AI model. - Processing is carried out exclusively on servers located within the European Union. - No transfer outside the EU is carried out. Regarding your data: Unless otherwise requested, your data is retained for a maximum of 2 years. In accordance with our internal security policies (PSSI) and current best practices, robust technical and organisational measures are implemented to protect the access and integrity of your information: secure access, rights management, encryption, security protocols, access monitoring, employee awareness, etc. Regarding your rights: In accordance with the GDPR, you have the right to access, rectify, object to and delete your data. You may exercise these rights by contacting dpo@septeo.com. Apply Please answer to all required questions. Mandatory fields are followed by * * Required fields Share job Our last jobs Chargé, chargée de scolarité M2 F/H Temporary contract\n- 6 months Full time Paris I apply Program office